 ```
 
+When `DISCORD_MENTION_ID` holds a valid Discord user snowflake (17-20 digits,
+surrounding whitespace trimmed), every alert ends with `<@USER_ID>` on its own
+line so the on-call gets a push notification. Anything else (`null`, empty,
+`@everyone`/`@here`, wrong length, embedded newlines or extra characters) is
+ignored silently with no mention. The 1800-character limit covers the whole
+content including the mention: long alerts truncate the title/message/context
+part so the mention survives.
+
 ## VPS target
 
 - VM **700899** (`103.199.186.228`), Ubuntu + Docker
